```java
@Service
public class IdempotencyService {
    private final IdempotencyRepository repo;
    private final ObjectMapper objectMapper;

    public String fingerprint(String operation, String actor, List<String> fields) {...}

    public <T> T execute(String requestId, String operation, String actor, List<String> fields,
                         int successStatus, Supplier<T> action) {
        String fp = fingerprint(operation, actor, fields);
        Optional<IdempotencyRecord> existing = repo.findByRequestId(requestId);
        if (existing.isPresent()) return replayOrConflict(existing.get(), fp);
        try {
            repo.insertPlaceholder(requestId, fp, operation, actor, Instant.now());
        } catch (DuplicateKeyException e) {
            return replayOrConflict(repo.findByRequestId(requestId).orElseThrow(), fp);
        }
        T result = action.get();
        repo.complete(requestId, successStatus, writeJson(result));
        return result;
    }
}
```

Wait, but replayOrConflict throws ReplayException or conflict; generic <T> — it never returns normally. Fine, declare `private <T> T replayOrConflict(...)` that always throws.

Hmm — one catch: the placeholder record, if the action later throws (business failure), the whole tx rolls back including placeholder. Good: "失败不占键".

